# Build context control.
#
# This repository holds ~94 GB of reference data and ~92 GB of results in the
# working tree. Docker copies the entire context to the daemon before running
# any instruction, so an exclude-everything-then-re-include policy is used:
# forgetting one large directory would otherwise stall every build.

# 1. Exclude everything.
*

# 2. Re-include only what the image needs.
!repogen/
!workflows/
!profiles/
!configs/
!envs/
!tests/
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# 3. Belt and braces: never ship data, outputs or VCS metadata even if a
#    re-include above is later broadened.
resources/
results/
logs/
figures/
paper_figures/
plot_examples/
reviews/
.git/
.github/
.venv/
.snakemake/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
tmp_*
_tmp_*
*.parquet
*.gctx
*.gz
